  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4dfe61d9-e41b-4918-8963-42c30a42f846-image.png\" style=\"width: 100px; height: 120px;\" /></p><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> be range of TV transmission.</p><p>From above figure,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8811;</mo><mo>&#8811;</mo><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8776;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, if coverage is to be increased <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> times</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Dividing equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mi>h</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>,&nbsp;then tower of height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is required.</p></blockquote>",
